## Third-party content

The MIT grant above covers this project's own source, configuration, and
documentation. The following bundled material is authored by others and carries
its own terms. Nothing here restricts the MIT grant on the rest of the project;
it records what the MIT grant does *not* reach.

### Bundled typefaces (`fonts/`)

Every bundled face is licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1, and
ships with its upstream license text alongside it in `fonts/`:

| Family | License file |
|---|---|
| Antonio | `fonts/Antonio-OFL.txt` |
| Astloch | `fonts/Astloch-OFL.txt` |
| Audiowide | `fonts/Audiowide-OFL.txt` |
| Cinzel | `fonts/Cinzel-OFL.txt` |
| Cormorant Garamond | `fonts/CormorantGaramond-OFL.txt` |
| DM Sans | `fonts/DMSans-OFL.txt` |
| Manufacturing Consent | `fonts/ManufacturingConsent-OFL.txt` |
| Orbitron | `fonts/Orbitron-OFL.txt` |
| Oxanium | `fonts/Oxanium-OFL.txt` |
| Playfair Display | `fonts/PlayfairDisplay-OFL.txt` |
| Plus Jakarta Sans | `fonts/PlusJakartaSans-OFL.txt` |
| Rajdhani | `fonts/Rajdhani-OFL.txt` |
| Righteous | `fonts/Righteous-OFL.txt` |
| Rye | `fonts/Rye-OFL.txt` |
| Share Tech Mono | `fonts/ShareTechMono-OFL.txt` |
| Space Grotesk | `fonts/SpaceGrotesk-OFL.txt` |
| Tangerine | `fonts/Tangerine-OFL.txt` |
| Weather Icons | `fonts/WeatherIcons-OFL.txt` |

The OFL requires that its text accompany the font, so a face added here without
its license file is a licensing defect, not a cosmetic omission. See
`docs/development.md` for the procedure when adding one.

### Images (`assets/`)

- `assets/moon_full.png` is an original lunar photograph by the copyright holder
  named above, and is covered by the MIT grant along with the rest of this
  project.
- `assets/banner.png` and everything under `assets/previews/` is generated by
  this project's own scripts (`scripts/build_banner.py`,
  `scripts/build_previews.py`, `scripts/build_split_previews.py`) and is
  likewise covered by the MIT grant.

### Quotation collection (`config/quotes.json`)

The bundled quote store is a curated collection of short quotations, many of
them from authors and works still in copyright, reproduced here as brief
attributed excerpts. The *selection, arrangement, and attribution data* are
covered by the MIT license above; the underlying quotations are not the
copyright holder's to license, and the MIT grant does not purport to convey any
rights in them. Redistributors relying on fair use or an equivalent exception
should make that assessment for themselves, and can replace the store entirely
via the `quotes.path` configuration key.

### Runtime dependencies

Dependencies are installed from PyPI rather than vendored, so none of their code
is redistributed in this repository. Two are worth naming because they are not
permissively licensed:

- `recurring-ical-events` — LGPL-3.0-or-later. Imported, never modified or
  bundled; anyone shipping a combined artifact (a container image, a frozen
  binary) should confirm they meet the LGPL's relinking condition.
- `caldav` — offered as GPL-3.0-or-later **or** Apache-2.0. This project relies
  on the Apache-2.0 election.

The Waveshare e-Paper driver is installed from its upstream repository by
`make pi-install` at setup time and is likewise not vendored here.
